From 41bae696ca77772ffe906505f0c04eb98bc7c9bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:19:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: ADSP remote heap
 no-map

The FastRPC change "misc: fastrpc: Allocate entire reserved memory for
Audio PD in probe" (9981fbe599e8 in linux-next) looks up the ADSP
channel's memory-region at rpmsg probe and assigns the whole range to
the LPASS and ADSP heap VMs with qcom_scm_assign_mem(), without
allocating it from the pool first.

Our region is a reusable shared-dma-pool, i.e. a CMA area: the page
allocator keeps placing movable Linux pages in it. Once the range has
been handed to the DSP VMs, the next access by Linux to such a page
faults at stage 2. The probe-time assignment is only safe for a region
Linux never maps or allocates from.

Make the region no-map (still dynamically placed below 4 GiB with the
same size and alignment), as hamoa.dtsi does with its static
adsp-rpc-remote-heap. Without 9981fbe599e8 the driver keeps working as
before: the region becomes a per-device coherent pool of the rpmsg
device, from which the Audio PD's heap is allocated and then assigned.

Cost: 12 MiB that Linux can no longer lend to movable allocations.

Fixes: 26752e27eac9 ("arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: add the ADSP FastRPC remote heap")
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index c6a36259d0..9b7dc78dfd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -324,13 +324,17 @@ llcc_lpi_mem: llcc-lpi@ff800000 {
 			no-map;
 		};
 
-		/* the ADSP FastRPC remote heap, as the vendor tree's adsp_heap_region */
+		/*
+		 * The ADSP FastRPC remote heap (the vendor tree's adsp_heap_region).
+		 * Not reusable: FastRPC hands the whole region to the LPASS and ADSP
+		 * heap VMs, so Linux must never place its own pages in it.
+		 */
 		adsp_rpc_remote_heap_mem: adsp-rpc-remote-heap {
 			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
 			alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x00000000 0x0 0xffffffff>;
-			reusable;
 			alignment = <0x0 0x400000>;
 			size = <0x0 0xc00000>;
+			no-map;
 		};
 	};
 
